[{:frontmatter
  {:id "adr-2607113500-kotobase-net-ingestion-cloud-itonami-lei"
   :title "ADR-2607113500: kotobase.net ingestion fold job for cloud-itonami-lei-* -- closes ADR-2607072300's open trigger-mechanism gap for this actor family"
   :status "accepted"
   :doc_type "adr"
   :topic "kotobase-net-ingestion-cloud-itonami-lei"
   :authoritative true
   :last_verified "2026-07-11"
   :authoritative_for
   ["For the cloud-itonami-lei-* actor family (ADR-2607110300), ADR-2607072300's open
     'journal -> kotobase-peer fold job' item is closed by a pull-based batch fold job
     (scripts/kotobase-ingest-cloud-itonami-lei.cljs, real nbb+cljs reusing
     kotoba-lang/kotobase-client verbatim), not a push-based webhook or a west-update hook"
    "kotobase.net's real production XRPC tx_edn wire format is a vector of ENTITY MAPS
     [{:db/id \"e\" :ns/attr v ...} ...], not [:db/add e a v] triples -- the latter is
     kotobase-peer's own in-process API shape (its README), not what kotobase-server's
     handler.cljc/tx-edn->quads accepts over the wire; discovered empirically via a real
     400 'kotobase: unrecognized tx_edn item' response, not assumed from ADR prose"
    "Idempotent re-ingestion is achieved by keyed cardinality-one upsert (same :db/id +
     attrs re-asserted), empirically verified (re-transacting one company left its :eavt
     datom count unchanged, not doubled)"
    "All 105 cloud-itonami-lei-* companies existing at ingestion time are live-queryable in
     kotobase.net today via a real multi-clause Datalog join, verified end to end"
    "The general 'every actor adopts the 80-data/public/*.journal.edn -> kotobase.net
     pattern' migration remains open exactly as ADR-2607072300 scoped it -- this ADR closes
     the gap for ONE actor family, not the general case"]
   :related
   ["90-docs/adr/2607072300-actor-public-data-git-journal-kotobase-index.md"
    "90-docs/adr/2607110300-cloud-itonami-lei-corporate-tos-catalog.md"
    "orgs/kotoba-lang/kotobase-client"
    "orgs/kotoba-lang/kotobase-peer"
    "orgs/gftdcojp/net-kotobase/kotobase-cf-wasm/DEPLOY.md"]
   :supersedes []
   :superseded_by []}

  :problem
  {:source "follow-up to ADR-2607110300: implement the kotobase.net ingestion job
            ADR-2607072300 explicitly left unimplemented, using the real
            cloud-itonami-lei-* corpus (105 real company ToS repos) as the concrete input"
   :investigated
   ["kotobase-peer (orgs/kotoba-lang/kotobase-peer) is a server-side library, not a
     deployed endpoint -- its README example tx-data shape ([:db/add e a v] vectors /
     {:s :p :o} maps) is its OWN in-process API, not necessarily the wire format any
     deployed XRPC server accepts"
    "the real production kotobase.net write/read surface is
     kotoba-lang/kotobase-server's handler.cljc, deployed via
     gftdcojp/net-kotobase/kotobase-cf-wasm at https://backend.kotobase.net (apex
     https://kotobase.net proxies /xrpc/* there per its own KOTOBA_BACKEND_URL var,
     confirmed live since 2026-07-08 per that repo's DEPLOY.md)"
    "kotobase-cf-wasm/wrangler.jsonc's production KOTOBASE_OPERATOR_DIDS var is empty
     (open allowlist) -- any self-minted CACAO whose issuer DID equals the graph owner
     can transact, no static pre-registration needed, confirmed by reading the actual
     deployed config, not assumed"
    "kotoba-lang/kotobase-client already has a complete, tested CACAO/transact/q/datoms
     client (src/kotobase/{client,cacao,cid}.cljs) matching the apex's exact auth shape
     (kotobase:pin capability + issuer-DID graph scope) -- confirmed runnable directly
     under nbb (no shadow-cljs compile step needed) by requiring it with --classpath"
    "first real transact attempt with [:db/add e a v] tx-data failed 400 InternalError
     with no detail via the apex; the same request against backend.kotobase.net directly
     surfaced 'kotobase: unrecognized tx_edn item', which led to reading
     kotobase-server's handler.cljc directly and finding tx-edn->quads only accepts
     entity maps (or [:db/retract ...]/[:db/retractEntity ...]), not [:db/add ...]"]
   :risk "assuming kotobase-peer's README example shape was the real wire format (without
          reading the actual server-side parser) would have produced a script that always
          400s in production while looking correct in isolation"}

  :decision
  {:trigger-mechanism
   {:choice "pull-based batch fold job"
    :why "the 105 cloud-itonami-lei-* repos are a static, already-existing set, not a live
          continuously-changing stream -- a script enumerating the org and fetching each
          repo's blueprint.edn + 80-data/public/tos.journal.edn via
          raw.githubusercontent.com (public repos, no auth needed) is simpler and correct
          for this shape; webhook/west-update-hook triggers are left as future work for
          actor families that grow continuously, matching ADR-2607072300's own deferral"}
   :implementation
   {:script "scripts/kotobase-ingest-cloud-itonami-lei.cljs"
    :runtime "nbb running real .cljs source (no shadow-cljs compile step) -- per root
              CLAUDE.md's runtime priority, a full Datalog engine has no cljs-native
              hosting runtime yet (kotobase-cf-wasm/DEPLOY.md's own finding), so nbb
              running real cljs is the correct current choice for this class of script"
    :reuse "requires kotoba-lang/kotobase-client's kotobase.client/kotobase.cacao/
            kotobase.cid verbatim via --classpath -- CACAO minting, did:key derivation,
            SIWE message construction, DAG-CBOR encoding are ALL reused unmodified, not
            reimplemented"
    :repo-enumeration "gh api \"orgs/cloud-itonami/repos\" --paginate (REST), not gh repo
                        list (GraphQL) -- GraphQL's session-wide rate limit was exhausted
                        mid-development by this session's earlier isic-family rollout;
                        REST has its own separate, much larger budget"}
   :identity
   {:did "did:key:z6Mkh6mnYrfXNjDSoRQfRK9a2QanvaSAVAqDFK44Vpss5ZSA"
    :graph_cid "bafyreifq6p445b472n6qbutttfaa3fegq5bbjnnxcmrogi5y6ksw46qwty"
    :db_name "cloud-itonami-lei-catalog"
    :secret-storage "scripts/.kotobase-ingest-cloud-itonami-lei-identity.hex, gitignored
                      via scripts/.gitignore, never committed -- same discipline as every
                      other actor's .<actor>/identity.edn per root CLAUDE.md"
    :operator-allowlist "empty/open in production (KOTOBASE_OPERATOR_DIDS=\"\" in
                          kotobase-cf-wasm/wrangler.jsonc) -- no static pre-registration
                          needed, self-sovereign per the existing CACAO actor pattern"
    :known-gap "the secret key exists ONLY as a local file in this session's environment
                -- not yet mirrored to 1Password/kagi like other actors' secrets
                typically are; losing this file before a future re-run would orphan a new,
                empty graph instead of continuing this one. Flagged as an honest follow-up,
                not resolved in this ADR."}
   :wire-format-correction
   {:wrong "[:db/add e a v] vectors (kotobase-peer's own in-process README example shape)"
    :right "a vector of entity maps [{:db/id \"e\" :ns/attr v ...} ...] -- the ONLY other
            accepted vector forms are [:db/retract e a v] (4-elem) and
            [:db/retractEntity e] (2-elem), per kotobase-server's handler.cljc
            tx-edn->quads dispatch, read directly from source, not inferred"
    :evidence "first attempt: POST https://backend.kotobase.net/xrpc/....transact with
               [:db/add e a v] tx_edn -> 400 {\"error\":\"InternalError\",\"message\":
               \"kotobase: unrecognized tx_edn item\"}. Corrected attempt with entity-map
               tx_edn -> 200 {\"ok\":true,\"commit\":\"bafyreif...\",\"datom_count\":1}"}
   :execution-result
   {:companies-attempted 105
    :companies-succeeded 105
    :companies-failed 0
    :per-company-facts ["blueprint.edn fields (:company/legal-name/:lei/:jurisdiction/
                          :website/:ticker) + :company/repo, on entity lei:<LEI>"
                         "one entity per distinct ToS doc-id in tos.journal.edn, carrying
                          :tos/full-text/:tos/source-url/:tos/retrieved-at/:tos/sha256/
                          :tos/doc-type + a :tos/company back-reference"]
    :idempotency-verification "re-transacted ExxonMobil's entity (lei:J3WHBG0MTS7O8ZVMDC91)
                                a second time; :eavt datom count for that entity stayed at
                                6 (not doubled to 12) -- confirmed via a real datoms call
                                after the re-transact, not assumed from cardinality-one
                                semantics alone"
    :read-verification "real multi-clause Datalog q against production:
                         {:find [?name ?url] :where [[?e :company/lei
                         \"J3WHBG0MTS7O8ZVMDC91\"] [?e :company/legal-name ?name]
                         [?tos :tos/company ?e] [?tos :tos/source-url ?url]]} returned
                         [[\"Exxon Mobil Corporation\"
                         \"https://corporate.exxonmobil.com/global-legal-pages/terms-and-conditions\"]]
                         -- a real join across two entity types round-tripped correctly"}}

  :consequences
  {:closes "ADR-2607072300's 'no ingestion pipeline code written' gap, for the
            cloud-itonami-lei-* family specifically -- the general 'every actor adopts
            this pattern' migration remains open, unchanged from that ADR's own scoping"
   :proves "kotobase.net (via backend.kotobase.net, the apex's real xrpc proxy target
             since the 2026-07-08 cutover) is a genuinely operational write/read surface,
             demonstrated with real data, not just a design on paper"
   :apex-note "https://kotobase.net apex serves a marketing page at / and returns 404 at
               /_health (its own routes, not proxied) -- only /xrpc/* is proxied to
               backend.kotobase.net per KOTOBA_BACKEND_URL; this script hits
               backend.kotobase.net directly to avoid depending on that proxy's exact
               behavior for non-xrpc paths"
   :follow-up-needed "persist the ingestion identity's secret key to a durable store
                       (1Password gftdcojp vault or kagi, matching other actors'
                       convention) before this session's local environment is lost --
                       explicitly NOT done in this ADR"
   :re-run-behavior "re-running the script for newly-added cloud-itonami-lei-* companies
                      (ADR-2607110300's rollout is ongoing) will ingest only the new ones
                      idempotently; there is no automatic trigger -- manual re-run, or a
                      future webhook/west-update-hook extension, out of this ADR's scope"}

  :alternatives
  [{:option "push-based webhook per cloud-itonami-lei-* repo"
    :rejected_because "infrastructure cost of a standing webhook listener isn't justified
                        for 105 static, already-existing repos; left as future work for
                        continuously-growing actor families, matching ADR-2607072300's own
                        not-decided deferral"}
   {:option "embed kotobase-peer's engine in-process (direct commit! calls) instead of
             going through the XRPC client"
    :rejected_because "kotobase-peer is a server-side library whose R2/B2 storage wiring,
                        CACAO verification, and IPNS head signing live in
                        kotobase-cf-wasm/kotobase-server -- this job is correctly an XRPC
                        client, not a second engine deployment"}
   {:option "compile a Node bundle via shadow-cljs instead of running via nbb"
    :rejected_because "empirically confirmed kotobase-client's real .cljs source runs
                        directly under nbb via --classpath with no compile step -- adding
                        a build pipeline had no justification once that was proven"}]}]
